    title: "France's welfare state is colliding with the bond market",
    excerpt: "Debt near 120% of GDP, an aging population, and repeated political resistance to reform are pushing French borrowing costs above former crisis countries—and turning a national budget problem into a euro-area risk.",
    lede: "France can still borrow, but investors are demanding more compensation. The warning is not that bankruptcy is imminent; it is that rising interest expense and weak political capacity are narrowing the government's room to preserve pensions and public services on existing terms.",
